 "notes": "No deviation in the registered protocol; one accounting note: the smoke used three rollouts (12,300 starts) where the estimate assumed two (8,200); total charged 621,402 of 640,000. Smoke passed first time (the widened-range module and the joint policy reproduce the parent in lockstep within 1e-5; the probe with threshold 6 rad/s and shifted residual coefficients changes actions and triggers more). All three arms ran 24 updates on seed 4998's placements with shared direction draws and physically matched module step sizes; terminal means frozen before confirmation; six policies confirmed once on twelve fresh manifests (seeds 4999-5010). Sustained success of 1,536: reference 661 (0.430), R-106 root 812 (0.529), CONTINUE parent 1,148 (0.747), MODULE_ORIGINAL 1,180 (0.768), MODULE_WIDE 1,192 (0.776), JOINT 1,238 (0.806); drops 80 / 49 / 76 / 82 / 75 / 70. Registered contrast JOINT minus MODULE_WIDE: +0.030 [+0.008, +0.052], Holm p 0.015, manifest-clustered [+0.020, +0.040], 171 wins and 125 losses: a positive co-adaptation effect is established, but the interval contains values on both sides of +0.05 (upper bound 0.0519), so the registered five-point magnitude is neither supported nor refuted. Boundary relief: MODULE_WIDE minus MODULE_ORIGINAL +0.008 [-0.004, +0.020] (not established). Every finalist qualifies under the registered rule (Holm p < 0.05 with a positive lower bound against both the CONTINUE parent and D-072, and drop bounds within 0.05 against both): MODULE_ORIGINAL +0.021 [+0.007, +0.034], MODULE_WIDE +0.029 [+0.016, +0.042], JOINT +0.059 [+0.035, +0.082] over the parent. Notable: training-time candidate success was flat for all three arms (about 0.72-0.76 throughout, on changing placements), yet all three finalists are better than the parent on fresh cases; the per-update means are averages over perturbed candidates and are a poor progress indicator. JOINT moved the residual by an L2 of 0.171 (largest single coefficient change 0.081) and its module ends with threshold 4.18 rad/s, ramp-out 6.3 steps, little-finger depth 0.0, stroke multiplier 1.45; discordance JOINT vs MODULE_WIDE was 296/1,536 = 0.19, three times the 0.064 anticipated, which is why the interval is wider than planned (SE 0.011). The CONTINUE parent replicates on new cases: +0.219 over the root (337 wins, 1 loss) and +0.317 over the reference. One matched set of ARS trajectories from one parent; a single confirmation."
